diff --git a/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md b/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md
index fdb7b9fa3..7834bc123 100644
--- a/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md
+++ b/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md
@@ -658,3 +658,18 @@ In the special case of `VK_SEMAPHORE_TYPE_TIMELINE` semaphores, **MoltenVK** will
 Makes MoltenVK treat all descriptors as if they had `VK_DESCRIPTOR_BINDING_PARTIALLY_BOUND_BIT` set.
 Versions of MoltenVK with this flag are less forgiving of applications that bind descriptors that point to
 destroyed objects, so this option can be used to temporarily work around any breakage that may have caused.
+
+
+---------------------------------------
+#### MVK_CONFIG_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HOST
+
+##### Type: Boolean
+##### Default: `1` (true)
+
+Controls whether MoltenVK advertises and enables the `VK_EXT_external_memory_host` device extension.
+
+When disabled (`0`), `VK_EXT_external_memory_host` is omitted from the advertised device extensions list,
+preventing clients (such as 32-bit Wine WoW64 / DXVK) from importing host-visible guest memory into
+no-copy Metal buffers that can trigger `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory` on Apple Silicon.
+Applications will transparently fall back to standard Vulkan device memory allocation.
